Great question and we respect it. Seeing is believing. The partnership is confirmed directly from VeChain's official 2026 Manifesto: "We proudly welcomed new business partners such as Lululemon China" — VeChain Official January 2026 http://vechain.org/vechains-2026-manifesto… The integration uses VeChain ToolChain — QR codes and NFC tags on products for authentication. The specific on-chain contract address for Lululemon is not publicly disclosed — enterprise clients typically operate through private ToolChain instances. But the transactions are real and verifiable on VeChainStats under ToolChain activity. http://vechainstats.com If anyone from the community can locate the specific address — please share below. We always verify before we post. 
@CoinIntelOrg
http://coinintel.org

Totally fair ask. Seeing is believing and you deserve a real answer. The partnership is confirmed via VeChain official Twitter and their 2026 Manifesto. The 100K+ transactions stat was specifically attributed to Rekord — not Lululemon. We made an error linking 100K+ transactions directly to Lululemon in our tweet. Rekord surpassed 100K on-chain transactions building Digital Product Passports on VeChain. Lululemon's on-chain activity runs through VeChain ToolChain and the specific contract address is not publicly disclosed. You can verify Rekord's transactions on http://vechainstats.com Thank you for pushing us to be more precise. This is exactly the standard 
@CoinIntelOrg
 holds itself to. We will correct our tweet.

