CHARGES LAID A man has been charged following an investigation into the trafficking & sale of stolen high-end merchandise from a Calgary retail store. On Tuesday, March 10, 2026, Lululemon security notified police that an individual was selling stolen merchandise on Facebook Marketplace for roughly half the original price. As the investigation progressed, officers identified the individual & executed a search warrant at his residence on Saturday, March 28, 2026. During the search, officers seized new Lululemon clothing, a significant number of forged identity documents & 17 pieces of stolen mail. As a result, Tyler Anthony CHASSE, 23, of Calgary, is charged with 23 offences, including: 1 count of possession of stolen property 1 count of trafficking stolen property 1 count of possession of proceeds of crime 2 counts of possession of stolen mail 18 counts of possession of forged documents CHASSE is scheduled to next appear in court on Friday, April 10, 2026. Retail crime may appear victimless, but it has real consequences for business owners & affects the overall sense of safety in our community. Fraud can also carry significant emotional & financial impacts & no one should feel embarrassed or alone in coming forward. Anyone who believes they may be a victim of fraud is encouraged to report it to the Calgary Police Service or Crime Stoppers. Anyone with information about this incident is asked to contact police. Information? CPS: 403-266-1234 
