Day 4/15 of creating AI ads until a brand hires me. Came across 
@oneractive
 of 
@KrissyCela3
 , a brand that doesn’t just sell activewear, it sells confidence, strength, and movement. My first thought wasn’t, “These are nice gym sets.” It was: “What if every step felt like a new version of you?” So I opened my AI tools and got to work. The idea was simple: One woman. One beautiful location. Six different Oner Active sets. No flashy transitions. No changing locations. Just effortless confidence, premium cinematography, and movement that lets the activewear speak for itself. Behind the scenes: • Researched Oner Active’s brand identity and visual language • Studied luxury activewear campaigns from brands like Apple, Alo Yoga, and Lululemon • Designed a bright, clean-girl environment inspired by modern California architecture • Created a consistent AI fitness model with a premium editorial look • Built a cinematic 6-scene storyboard with six distinct personalities • Animated each scene using AI while maintaining character consistency and realistic fabric physics What started as a fitness brand I admired became a cinematic AI fashion campaign. That’s what excites me about AI. It’s not just about generating beautiful visuals. It’s about understanding a brand’s identity and translating it into a story that feels authentic. I’m building my AI commercial portfolio in public, one brand at a time. If you’re building a fashion, beauty, fitness, or lifestyle brand and you’ve ever wondered, “What would my next campaign look like if AI handled the production?” I’d love to show you. Your next customer could be one scroll away. P.S. 
@oneractive
 has one of the cleanest visual identities in activewear, and it was a fun challenge imagining how that aesthetic could come to life through an AI-powered commercial.

