@CressTopStocks
 joins Nicole Benjamin to reveal why its massive decline is backed by cold, hard data. The Key Warning Signs: - Underperforming Growth: Lululemon's growth grade has plummeted to a "D" relative to its sector peers. - Bottom-Tier Momentum: With an "F" grade in momentum, its price performance is drastically lagging behind the rest of the consumer discretionary sector. - Something Is Wrong: When a major brand underperforms its sector this heavily, it's a structural sign of wrong products or slowing execution. - Steven’s Take: "I think there's three investment characteristics that indicate you really need to stay away from the stock... and if you own it, maybe even consider selling it". #Investing#StockMarket#Lululemon#LULU#ConsumerDiscretionary#SeekingAlpha Watch the full quantitative factor breakdown below!

